# W05.3.1 — native worker-base whole-HU carry calibration

This is a static local calibration for the existing P02 picker identity and the unchanged worker-base GLB. It is not a pickup, a stock-location change, a loaded walk, packing, a Scene binding, a reservation or an engine operation. The calibration fixture contains one body and one whole SMALL_CARTON template; no object is added to the warehouse. The frozen upstream population remains24 actors,2 vehicles and530 HUs.

The example is the original whole `v3:HU:initial:DEMO_067:01`:24 units, .94kg, .32×.24×.24m. Its original assignment is read only. The calibration places the cargo bottom at worker-local[0,.96,.52], yaw0 and scale1. The solved lower-pad reference points are[±.16,1.08,.44]. Their horizontal radius from the declared worker-root frame is approximately.468188m, within the source.4712m manual grasp rule; height1.08m is below1.25m. The cargo-centre horizontal distance.52m is separately reported and is not the grasp distance. The synthetic15kg boundary is not a legal, strength or ergonomic certification.

Worker-base has neither the manual asset's additional shoulder lift, elbow swivel nor movable fingers. Only its existing upper-arm XYZ, forearm XYZ, palm-roll Y and wrist XYZ rotations are solved, within the original GLB metadata and dimension-spec limits. Other native transforms, scale, body position, head, lower body and foot stance remain exactly at source rest. The existing manual carry JSON supplies an initial search reference only. A fixed base-rig branch seed records a reproducible result of the bounded search; forward kinematics are independently checked against the actual GLTFLoader hierarchy and actual native surfaces.

The solver checks two nonzero-area native lower-pad patches against actual opposed SMALL_CARTON side triangles. Plane gaps and nearest native triangle distances must be≤2 micrometres; native normals must oppose. It checks every body triangle against the whole cargo envelope shrunk by2 micrometres, plus whole-mesh solid-angle/depth penetration witnesses. C-mouth tests use actual forearm/cuff triangles in each native hand frame and the original mouth box shrunk by2 micrometres, including whole-mesh containment.

All visible physical body meshes participate in baseline/current self checks. Connected components prune AABBs only; winding/depth use each entire original native mesh, including every disconnected solid. Changed nonadjacent arm/body witnesses block admission, including forearm→torso, upper arm→head and arm→opposite arm. Original same-frame model joins and observed adjacent physical-joint mesh pairs are retained explicitly with witnesses and baseline comparison; they are not a zero-intersection claim. Same-mesh baked joins are rigid and unchanged. Newly generated role-badge ink is decorative; its original physical badge base remains checked. Triangle-centroid inward probes and native edge/triangle crossing probes are bounded evidence, not an exhaustive collision certificate.

Controls deliberately move the actual cargo by20 micrometres to lose contact, move it into the actual head to produce a whole-native shared-interior witness, and reproduce the rejected central-thumb/HU collision. Exact repeated application, apply(0), source-pose restoration, geometry/index/metadata identity, native foot-floor contact and deterministic full recomputation are checked. Invalid primitive types, bool/nonfinite values, extra/omitted joints, manual-only pivots, changed IDs, dimensions, counts, mass, scale and source fingerprints are rejected independently of solver success.

From `frontend`, run `node tools/solve-worker-base-carry-v3.mjs`, then the same command with `--check-only`. Check-only recomputes native geometry, constraints and controls and compares exact expected pose/report bytes; it does not refresh fingerprints or write files. Only the new pose and W05.3.1 report are emitted by a normal run. The script refuses source drift before publishing. No registry/profile/fixture/sourcepack dependency is created; population and cargo identity come from frozen upstream contracts, catalogue and baseline assignment.

Root owns visual review and subsequent acceptance. Pickup/withdrawal, actual P02 source approach, loaded gait and turns, same-HU setdown, destination packing preparation, shared resource ownership and Scene integration remain separate W05.3 work.
